Below is a summary of what’s happening and how we’re going to fix it:

Issue in a nutshell  
– TooltipIcon shows its tooltip on both focus and hover.  
– When you click (focus) one icon‐only button, its tooltip stays visible.  
– Hovering a second icon then shows *two* tooltips at once.  

We don’t have any simple cross‐component way of telling the first TooltipIcon to hide itself when a second one is hovered, so the easiest, least‐invasive fix is to stop showing the tooltip on focus altogether. In short, drop the focus‐to‐show behavior for icon‐only buttons (relying on aria‐labels for accessibility instead), and keep only the hover behavior.

Below are two *SEARCH/REPLACE* edits for `packages/react/src/components/TooltipIcon/TooltipIcon.js` that:

1. Remove the `onFocus` prop from the component API (and its handler).  
2. Remove the `<button onFocus=…>` binding so that focus no longer shows the tooltip.

